-- title:
--   Definitions for Calibrated representations of affine Hecke algebras
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Calibrated representations of affine Hecke algebras* (arXiv:math/0401323) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `Datum`: Finite, reduced, irreducible crystallographic root data, with the full weight lattice identified with `Z^rank` by evaluation on the simple coroots (PDF pp.3--4). The connectedness condition is irreducibility of the Dynkin diagram.
--   - `FullWeightLattice`: The FULL weight lattice, in fundamental-weight coordinates, PDF p.4.
--   - `Weyl`: The finite Weyl group constructed from the root datum, PDF p.3.
--   - `simpleRootWeight`: Simple root as a vector in the full weight lattice, PDF p.4.
--   - `simple`: The actual simple reflection, not an unrelated permutation, PDF p.3.
--   - `GoodParameter`: Nonzero parameter which is not a root of unity, PDF p.3.
--   - `Torus`: Multiplicative complex characters of the full weight lattice, PDF p.4.
--   - `torusCharacterEval`: Evaluation of the character on `X^lambda`, PDF p.4.
--   - `weylCharacter`: Contragredient Weyl action `(w t)(X^lambda)=t(X^(w^-1 lambda))`, PDF p.4.
--   - `characterOrbit`: The Weyl orbit of a character, PDF p.6.
--   - `positive`: Positive roots, with the base chosen in the datum, PDF p.3.
--   - `inversions`: The inversion set `R(w)`, PDF p.10.
--   - `zeroRoots`: The positive roots vanishing at the character, PDF p.10.
--   - `poleRoots`: The positive roots evaluated at `q^2` or `q^-2`, PDF p.10.
--   - `tableaux`: Canonical standard tableaux: these are Weyl elements, not orbit points, PDF p.10.
--   - `tableauWeights`: The image of the tableaux in the orbit, PDF pp.10--11.
--   - `PlacedShape`: Placed shapes have a nonempty set of standard tableaux, PDF p.10.
--   - `CalibrationEdge`: Distinct-endpoint calibration edges, symmetrized to avoid choosing an orientation, PDF p.10. The graph on an orbit is the induced graph on that orbit.
--   - `Connected`: Connection by a finite edge path; a vertex connects to itself, PDF p.10.
--   - `rankTwoWeyl`: The parabolic rank-two Weyl group, PDF p.11.
--   - `rankTwoRoots`: The rank-two subsystem generated by two distinct simple roots, PDF p.11.
--   - `ExceptionalCalibration`: The exceptional C2/G2 calibration condition, with `i` the long root, PDF p.11. The ordered Cartan entries distinguish long and short roots.
--   - `Calibratable`: Rank-two calibratability, including both choices of the long root, PDF p.11.
--   - `PlacedSkewShape`: Placed skew shape, PDF pp.11--12. The explicit simple-root regularity is the proof-supported rank-one repair: printed rank-two conditions alone are vacuous in A1, where they would allow a zero denominator.
--   - `HeckeGenerators`: A left generator action. Relation satisfaction is a separate predicate; it is a conclusion, rather than an assumption, for the explicit construction.
--   - `alternating`: Alternating words are written in multiplication order; operators act rightmost first.
--   - `braidLength`: Coxeter braid length is the order of `s_i s_j`, correcting the Cartan-product misprint on PDF p.3.
--   - `dividedDifference`: Polynomial divided difference in (1.2), including negative weight coordinates, PDF p.4. There is no division by an algebra element.
--   - `Relations`: Exactly the generator relations of the affine Hecke algebra, PDF pp.3--4. Thus an action satisfying this predicate is precisely a left module over the algebra presented there, without assuming a PBW theorem.
--   - `weightSpace`: Simultaneous ordinary eigenspace, PDF p.5.
--   - `genSpace`: Simultaneous generalized eigenspace, PDF p.5. Each lattice element has its own nilpotence exponent, as in the source; no diagonalizability is assumed.
--   - `generalizedSupport`: Generalized-weight support, PDF p.5.
--   - `weightSupport`: Ordinary-weight support, used to index the basis in Proposition 4.1, PDF p.15.
--   - `Calibrated`: Calibration is equality of generalized and ordinary weight spaces, PDF p.14.
--   - `HeckeIrreducible`: Nonzero irreducibility, independently of any weight-space conclusions, PDF pp.5--6. Invariant subspaces must be invariant under every generator.
--   - `CentralCharacter`: Central character: the invariant Laurent-polynomial subalgebra acts by its evaluation at `t`, the convention on PDF p.6 (using Theorem 1.3).
--   - `HeckeEquivalent`: Representation equivalence intertwines both sets of generators, PDF p.18.
--   - `seminormalDiagonal`: Diagonal coefficient, using the negative-root denominator of the actual tau definition and Theorem 3.1, PDF pp.7,12.
--   - `weightMatrixEntry`: Zero-extended matrix coefficient in an occurring-weight basis, PDF pp.15--16. Missing weights have coefficient zero; their diagonal scalar is still `seminormalDiagonal`.
--   - `localInverse`: Finite geometric-series inverse of `1-X^lambda` on the generalized t-space, PDF p.7. It is used only when `t(X^lambda) != 1`; the exponent bound is the ambient finite dimension, so this definition retains Jordan nilpotents.
--   - `localIntertwiner`: Local tau formula, extended polynomially to the ambient space for typing. Only its restriction to the generalized t-space is asserted to be the source's local map, and only on the stated nonvanishing domain, PDF p.7.
--   - `wordWeyl`: Weyl element of a word, in multiplication order.
--   - `TauWordDefined`: All the local tau factors are defined at their successive incoming weights. Products act rightmost first, as in Proposition 2.7(e), PDF pp.7--9.
--   - `tauWord`: A word of local tau operators, with the correct weight for every factor.
--   - `tauSquare`: The rational square in Proposition 2.7(c), evaluated as local operators, PDF pp.7--8. Both denominators are inverted on the generalized weight space.
--   - `TableauSpace`: The free complex vector space on the actual standard tableaux, PDF p.12.
--   - `tableauVector`: The basis vector labelled by w; it is zero if w is not a standard tableau, exactly the convention in Theorem 3.1, PDF p.12.
--   - `tableauGenerators`: The explicitly constructed operators of Theorem 3.1, PDF p.12. No relations, irreducibility or calibration are assumed here.
-- source:
--   Calibrated representations of affine Hecke algebras, arXiv:math/0401323v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0401323v2

import Mathlib

/-!
Statements from Arun Ram, Calibrated representations of affine Hecke algebras,
arXiv:math/0401323v2. The local operator presentation below is the Bernstein
presentation on the FULL weight lattice, in fundamental-weight coordinates.
No assertion about a principal series or rational PBW expansion is hidden in
these definitions. Those targets are deferred in the accompanying inventory.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P26

open scoped BigOperators

/-- Finite, reduced, irreducible crystallographic root data, with the full weight
lattice identified with `Z^rank` by evaluation on the simple coroots (PDF pp.3--4).
The connectedness condition is irreducibility of the Dynkin diagram. -/
structure Datum where
  rank : ℕ
  rank_pos : 0 < rank
  rootCount : ℕ
  pairing : RootPairing (Fin rootCount) ℤ (Fin rank → ℤ) (Fin rank → ℤ)
  reduced : pairing.IsReduced
  base : pairing.Base
  simpleIndex : Fin rank ≃ base.support
  fullWeightLattice : ∀ (x : Fin rank → ℤ) (i : Fin rank),
    pairing.toLinearMap x (pairing.coroot (simpleIndex i)) = x i
  irreducible : ∀ S : Set (Fin rank), S.Nonempty → Sᶜ.Nonempty →
    ∃ i ∈ S, ∃ j ∈ Sᶜ,
      pairing.pairing (simpleIndex i) (simpleIndex j) ≠ 0
  finiteW : Finite pairing.weylGroup

attribute [instance] Datum.finiteW

/-- The FULL weight lattice, in fundamental-weight coordinates, PDF p.4. -/
abbrev FullWeightLattice (D : Datum) := Fin D.rank → ℤ

/-- The finite Weyl group constructed from the root datum, PDF p.3. -/
abbrev Weyl (D : Datum) := D.pairing.weylGroup

/-- The canonical finite enumeration of the finite Weyl group, PDF p.3. -/
noncomputable instance weylFintype (D : Datum) : Fintype (Weyl D) := Fintype.ofFinite _

/-- Simple root as a vector in the full weight lattice, PDF p.4. -/
def simpleRootWeight (D : Datum) (i : Fin D.rank) : FullWeightLattice D :=
  D.pairing.root (D.simpleIndex i)

/-- The actual simple reflection, not an unrelated permutation, PDF p.3. -/
def simple (D : Datum) (i : Fin D.rank) : Weyl D :=
  RootPairing.weylGroup.ofIdx D.pairing (D.simpleIndex i)

/-- Nonzero parameter which is not a root of unity, PDF p.3. -/
def GoodParameter (q : ℂ) : Prop := q ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → q ^ k ≠ 1

/-- Multiplicative complex characters of the full weight lattice, PDF p.4. -/
abbrev Torus (D : Datum) := Multiplicative (FullWeightLattice D) →* ℂˣ

/-- Evaluation of the character on `X^lambda`, PDF p.4. -/
def torusCharacterEval {D : Datum} (t : Torus D) (x : FullWeightLattice D) : ℂ :=
  (t (Multiplicative.ofAdd x) : ℂ)

/-- Contragredient Weyl action `(w t)(X^lambda)=t(X^(w^-1 lambda))`, PDF p.4. -/
def weylCharacter (D : Datum) (w : Weyl D) (t : Torus D) : Torus D where
  toFun x := t (Multiplicative.ofAdd (w⁻¹ • Multiplicative.toAdd x))
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' := by intro x y; simp [smul_add]

/-- The Weyl orbit of a character, PDF p.6. -/
def characterOrbit (D : Datum) (t : Torus D) : Set (Torus D) := Set.range (fun w => weylCharacter D w t)

/-- Positive roots, with the base chosen in the datum, PDF p.3. -/
def positive (D : Datum) : Set (Fin D.rootCount) := {a | D.base.IsPos a}

/-- The inversion set `R(w)`, PDF p.10. -/
def inversions (D : Datum) (w : Weyl D) : Set (Fin D.rootCount) :=
  {a | a ∈ positive D ∧ ¬ D.base.IsPos (D.pairing.weylGroupToPerm w a)}

/-- The positive roots vanishing at the character, PDF p.10. -/
def zeroRoots (D : Datum) (t : Torus D) : Set (Fin D.rootCount) :=
  {a | a ∈ positive D ∧ torusCharacterEval t (D.pairing.root a) = 1}

/-- The positive roots evaluated at `q^2` or `q^-2`, PDF p.10. -/
def poleRoots (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) : Set (Fin D.rootCount) :=
  {a | a ∈ positive D ∧
    (torusCharacterEval t (D.pairing.root a) = q ^ 2 ∨ torusCharacterEval t (D.pairing.root a) = (q⁻¹) ^ 2)}

/-- Canonical standard tableaux: these are Weyl elements, not orbit points, PDF p.10. -/
def tableaux (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)) :
    Set (Weyl D) :=
  {w | inversions D w ∩ zeroRoots D t = ∅ ∧ inversions D w ∩ poleRoots D q t = J}

/-- The image of the tableaux in the orbit, PDF pp.10--11. -/
def tableauWeights (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)) :
    Set (Torus D) := (fun w => weylCharacter D w t) '' tableaux D q t J

/-- Placed shapes have a nonempty set of standard tableaux, PDF p.10. -/
def PlacedShape (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)) : Prop :=
  J ⊆ poleRoots D q t ∧ (tableaux D q t J).Nonempty

/-- Distinct-endpoint calibration edges, symmetrized to avoid choosing an orientation,
PDF p.10. The graph on an orbit is the induced graph on that orbit. -/
def CalibrationEdge (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t u : Torus D) : Prop :=
  t ≠ u ∧ ∃ i : Fin D.rank,
    (u = weylCharacter D (simple D i) t ∧ torusCharacterEval t (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ q ^ 2 ∧
      torusCharacterEval t (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ (q⁻¹) ^ 2) ∨
    (t = weylCharacter D (simple D i) u ∧ torusCharacterEval u (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ q ^ 2 ∧
      torusCharacterEval u (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ (q⁻¹) ^ 2)

/-- Connection by a finite edge path; a vertex connects to itself, PDF p.10. -/
def Connected (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t u : Torus D) : Prop :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen (CalibrationEdge D q) t u

/-- The parabolic rank-two Weyl group, PDF p.11. -/
def rankTwoWeyl (D : Datum) (i j : Fin D.rank) : Subgroup (Weyl D) :=
  Subgroup.closure {simple D i, simple D j}

/-- The rank-two subsystem generated by two distinct simple roots, PDF p.11. -/
def rankTwoRoots (D : Datum) (i j : Fin D.rank) : Set (Fin D.rootCount) :=
  {a | D.pairing.root a ∈ Submodule.span ℤ {simpleRootWeight D i, simpleRootWeight D j}}

/-- The exceptional C2/G2 calibration condition, with `i` the long root,
PDF p.11. The ordered Cartan entries distinguish long and short roots. -/
def ExceptionalCalibration (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (i j : Fin D.rank) : Prop :=
  (D.pairing.pairing (D.simpleIndex i) (D.simpleIndex j) = -2 ∨
   D.pairing.pairing (D.simpleIndex i) (D.simpleIndex j) = -3) ∧
  D.pairing.pairing (D.simpleIndex j) (D.simpleIndex i) = -1 ∧
  torusCharacterEval t (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ 1 ∧ torusCharacterEval t (simpleRootWeight D j) ≠ 1 ∧
  ∃ u : rankTwoWeyl D i j,
    torusCharacterEval (weylCharacter D u.val t) (simpleRootWeight D i) = q ^ 2 ∧
    torusCharacterEval (weylCharacter D u.val t) (simpleRootWeight D j) = 1

/-- Rank-two calibratability, including both choices of the long root, PDF p.11. -/
def Calibratable (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (i j : Fin D.rank) : Prop :=
  (∀ a ∈ rankTwoRoots D i j, torusCharacterEval t (D.pairing.root a) ≠ 1) ∨
  ExceptionalCalibration D q t i j ∨ ExceptionalCalibration D q t j i

/-- Placed skew shape, PDF pp.11--12. The explicit simple-root regularity
is the proof-supported rank-one repair: printed rank-two conditions alone
are vacuous in A1, where they would allow a zero denominator. -/
def PlacedSkewShape (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D)
    (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)) : Prop :=
  PlacedShape D q t J ∧ ∀ w ∈ tableaux D q t J,
    (∀ i, torusCharacterEval (weylCharacter D w t) (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ 1) ∧
    (∀ i j, i ≠ j → Calibratable D q (weylCharacter D w t) i j)

variable {D : Datum} {V U : Type*}
variable [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [AddCommGroup U] [Module ℂ U]

/-- A left generator action. Relation satisfaction is a separate predicate;
it is a conclusion, rather than an assumption, for the explicit construction. -/
structure HeckeGenerators (D : Datum) (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] where
  X : FullWeightLattice D → Module.End ℂ V
  T : Fin D.rank → Module.End ℂ V

/-- Alternating words are written in multiplication order; operators act rightmost first. -/
def alternating {n : ℕ} (i j : Fin n) (m : ℕ) : List (Fin n) :=
  (List.range m).map (fun k => if k % 2 = 0 then i else j)

/-- Coxeter braid length is the order of `s_i s_j`, correcting the Cartan-product
misprint on PDF p.3. -/
def braidLength (D : Datum) (i j : Fin D.rank) : ℕ :=
  orderOf (simple D i * simple D j)

/-- Polynomial divided difference in (1.2), including negative weight coordinates,
PDF p.4. There is no division by an algebra element. -/
def dividedDifference (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (i : Fin D.rank) (x : FullWeightLattice D) :
    Module.End ℂ V :=
  if 0 ≤ x i then
    ∑ r ∈ Finset.range (x i).toNat, A.X (x - (r : ℤ) • simpleRootWeight D i)
  else
    -(∑ r ∈ Finset.range (-x i).toNat, A.X (x + ((r : ℤ) + 1) • simpleRootWeight D i))

/-- Exactly the generator relations of the affine Hecke algebra, PDF pp.3--4.
Thus an action satisfying this predicate is precisely a left module over the
algebra presented there, without assuming a PBW theorem. -/
def Relations (q : ℂ) (A : HeckeGenerators D V) : Prop :=
  A.X 0 = 1 ∧
  (∀ x y, A.X (x + y) = A.X x * A.X y) ∧
  (∀ i, A.T i * A.T i = (q - q⁻¹) • A.T i + 1) ∧
  (∀ i j, i ≠ j →
    ((alternating i j (braidLength D i j)).map A.T).prod =
    ((alternating j i (braidLength D i j)).map A.T).prod) ∧
  (∀ i x, A.X x * A.T i = A.T i * A.X (simple D i • x) +
    (q - q⁻¹) • dividedDifference A i x)

/-- Simultaneous ordinary eigenspace, PDF p.5. -/
def weightSpace (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (t : Torus D) : Submodule ℂ V :=
  ⨅ x : FullWeightLattice D, LinearMap.ker (A.X x - torusCharacterEval t x • (1 : Module.End ℂ V))

/-- Simultaneous generalized eigenspace, PDF p.5. Each lattice element has
its own nilpotence exponent, as in the source; no diagonalizability is assumed. -/
def genSpace (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (t : Torus D) : Submodule ℂ V :=
  ⨅ x : FullWeightLattice D, (A.X x).maxGenEigenspace (torusCharacterEval t x)

/-- Generalized-weight support, PDF p.5. -/
def generalizedSupport (A : HeckeGenerators D V) : Set (Torus D) := {t | genSpace A t ≠ ⊥}

/-- Ordinary-weight support, used to index the basis in Proposition 4.1, PDF p.15. -/
def weightSupport (A : HeckeGenerators D V) : Set (Torus D) := {t | weightSpace A t ≠ ⊥}

/-- Calibration is equality of generalized and ordinary weight spaces, PDF p.14. -/
def Calibrated (A : HeckeGenerators D V) : Prop := ∀ t, genSpace A t = weightSpace A t

/-- Nonzero irreducibility, independently of any weight-space conclusions,
PDF pp.5--6. Invariant subspaces must be invariant under every generator. -/
def HeckeIrreducible (A : HeckeGenerators D V) : Prop :=
  Nontrivial V ∧ ∀ S : Submodule ℂ V,
    (∀ x m, m ∈ S → A.X x m ∈ S) →
    (∀ i m, m ∈ S → A.T i m ∈ S) → S = ⊥ ∨ S = ⊤

/-- Central character: the invariant Laurent-polynomial subalgebra acts by
its evaluation at `t`, the convention on PDF p.6 (using Theorem 1.3). -/
def CentralCharacter (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (t : Torus D) : Prop :=
  ∀ f : FullWeightLattice D →₀ ℂ,
    (∀ (w : Weyl D) x, f (w • x) = f x) →
    f.sum (fun x c => c • A.X x) =
      (f.sum (fun x c => c * torusCharacterEval t x)) • (1 : Module.End ℂ V)

/-- Representation equivalence intertwines both sets of generators, PDF p.18. -/
def HeckeEquivalent (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (B : HeckeGenerators D U) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : V ≃ₗ[ℂ] U,
    (∀ x m, e (A.X x m) = B.X x (e m)) ∧
    (∀ i m, e (A.T i m) = B.T i (e m))

/-- Diagonal coefficient, using the negative-root denominator of the actual
tau definition and Theorem 3.1, PDF pp.7,12. -/
def seminormalDiagonal (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (i : Fin D.rank) : ℂ :=
  (q - q⁻¹) / (1 - torusCharacterEval t (-simpleRootWeight D i))

/-- Zero-extended matrix coefficient in an occurring-weight basis, PDF pp.15--16.
Missing weights have coefficient zero; their diagonal scalar is still `seminormalDiagonal`. -/
def weightMatrixEntry (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (b : Module.Basis (weightSupport A) ℂ V)
    (i : Fin D.rank) (c t : Torus D) : ℂ := by
  classical
  exact if ht : t ∈ weightSupport A then
    if hc : c ∈ weightSupport A then b.repr (A.T i (b ⟨t, ht⟩)) ⟨c, hc⟩ else 0
  else 0

/-- Finite geometric-series inverse of `1-X^lambda` on the generalized t-space,
PDF p.7. It is used only when `t(X^lambda) != 1`; the exponent bound is the
ambient finite dimension, so this definition retains Jordan nilpotents. -/
def localInverse [FiniteDimensional ℂ V] (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (t : Torus D)
    (x : FullWeightLattice D) : Module.End ℂ V :=
  ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (Module.finrank ℂ V),
    ((1 - torusCharacterEval t x)⁻¹ ^ (k + 1)) •
      (A.X x - torusCharacterEval t x • (1 : Module.End ℂ V)) ^ k

/-- Local tau formula, extended polynomially to the ambient space for typing.
Only its restriction to the generalized t-space is asserted to be the source's
local map, and only on the stated nonvanishing domain, PDF p.7. -/
def localIntertwiner [FiniteDimensional ℂ V] (q : ℂ) (A : HeckeGenerators D V)
    (t : Torus D) (i : Fin D.rank) : Module.End ℂ V :=
  A.T i - (q - q⁻¹) • localInverse A t (-simpleRootWeight D i)

/-- Weyl element of a word, in multiplication order. -/
def wordWeyl (D : Datum) (word : List (Fin D.rank)) : Weyl D :=
  (word.map (simple D)).prod

/-- All the local tau factors are defined at their successive incoming weights.
Products act rightmost first, as in Proposition 2.7(e), PDF pp.7--9. -/
def TauWordDefined (D : Datum) (t : Torus D) : List (Fin D.rank) → Prop
  | [] => True
  | i :: rest => TauWordDefined D t rest ∧
      torusCharacterEval (weylCharacter D (wordWeyl D rest) t) (simpleRootWeight D i) ≠ 1

/-- A word of local tau operators, with the correct weight for every factor. -/
def tauWord [FiniteDimensional ℂ V] (q : ℂ) (A : HeckeGenerators D V)
    (t : Torus D) : List (Fin D.rank) → Module.End ℂ V
  | [] => 1
  | i :: rest => localIntertwiner q A (weylCharacter D (wordWeyl D rest) t) i * tauWord q A t rest

/-- The rational square in Proposition 2.7(c), evaluated as local operators,
PDF pp.7--8. Both denominators are inverted on the generalized weight space. -/
def tauSquare [FiniteDimensional ℂ V] (q : ℂ) (A : HeckeGenerators D V)
    (t : Torus D) (i : Fin D.rank) : Module.End ℂ V :=
  ((q • (1 : Module.End ℂ V) - q⁻¹ • A.X (simpleRootWeight D i)) *
    (q • (1 : Module.End ℂ V) - q⁻¹ • A.X (-simpleRootWeight D i))) *
    (localInverse A t (simpleRootWeight D i) * localInverse A t (-simpleRootWeight D i))

/-- The free complex vector space on the actual standard tableaux, PDF p.12. -/
abbrev TableauSpace (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)) :=
  {w : Weyl D // w ∈ tableaux D q t J} →₀ ℂ

/-- The basis vector labelled by w; it is zero if w is not a standard tableau,
exactly the convention in Theorem 3.1, PDF p.12. -/
def tableauVector (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount))
    (w : Weyl D) : TableauSpace D q t J := by
  classical
  exact if h : w ∈ tableaux D q t J then Finsupp.single ⟨w, h⟩ 1 else 0

/-- The explicitly constructed operators of Theorem 3.1, PDF p.12.
No relations, irreducibility or calibration are assumed here. -/
def tableauGenerators (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)) :
    HeckeGenerators D (TableauSpace D q t J) where
  X x := Finsupp.linearCombination ℂ (fun w =>
    torusCharacterEval (weylCharacter D w.val t) x • Finsupp.single w 1)
  T i := Finsupp.linearCombination ℂ (fun w =>
    seminormalDiagonal q (weylCharacter D w.val t) i • Finsupp.single w 1 +
    (q⁻¹ + seminormalDiagonal q (weylCharacter D w.val t) i) • tableauVector D q t J (simple D i * w.val))

/-- Sanity: the character of the identity monomial is one, including rank one. -/
example (D : Datum) (t : Torus D) : torusCharacterEval t 0 = 1 := by
  simp [torusCharacterEval]

/-- Sanity: reflexive paths do not require any edge or denominator. -/
example (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) : Connected D q t t :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen.refl

/-- Sanity: the empty local-operator word is the identity. -/
example [FiniteDimensional ℂ V] (q : ℂ) (A : HeckeGenerators D V) (t : Torus D) :
    tauWord q A t [] = 1 := rfl

/-- Sanity: a missing tableau is sent to the zero vector, PDF p.12. -/
example (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount))
    (w : Weyl D) (h : w ∉ tableaux D q t J) : tableauVector D q t J w = 0 := by
  simp [tableauVector, h]

/-- Sanity: X acts on each labelled basis vector by the displayed character. -/
example (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount))
    (w : {w : Weyl D // w ∈ tableaux D q t J}) (x : FullWeightLattice D) :
    (tableauGenerators D q t J).X x (Finsupp.single w 1) =
      torusCharacterEval (weylCharacter D w.val t) x • Finsupp.single w 1 := by
  simp [tableauGenerators]

/-- Sanity: in dimension one the local inverse is the ordinary scalar reciprocal. -/
example (A : HeckeGenerators D ℂ) (t : Torus D) (x : FullWeightLattice D) :
    localInverse A t x = (1 - torusCharacterEval t x)⁻¹ • (1 : Module.End ℂ ℂ) := by
  simp [localInverse]

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P26


